                             Uni-UserList v2.2
                             -----------------
                Written by Ray Akey for C-Net Amiga v3.05+

Changes v2.2
------------
1. Fixed output problem with Computer types.
2. Added Organization and Banner to output list.
3. Fixed bug where '\' was printed when used to abort.

Changes v2.1
------------
1. Recompiled for CNet/3.05.

Changes v2.0
-------------
1. Added OutPut to FILE option.  Full removal of any MCI before text is
   written to your output file.  "Output to file" may be toggled on or off.


Installation:
-------------
1. Copy Uni-UserList to PFILES:
2. Copy Uni-Listtext to SYSTEXT:
3. "AO" to your pfiles as a CNet pfile.

           ** AND/OR **

   Add the following line to BBSMENU at END of the "Main" or "Everywhere"
   commands if you wish to call uni-userlist as a menu option:

	UUL	|\#2Pfiles:Uni-UserList\

   The SYSTEXT:uni-listtext file is editable in the same manner as bbstext.

Program Options:
----------------
  Following is a short, but fairly detailed explanation of the functions.

[S]earch
--------
  Simply a pattern search for the following types of data, each selectable
before listing:

  Handle
  Access
  Data Phone #
  Address
  City
  Computer Type
  Zip Code
  Baudrate

  MUCH more work will be going into this "SEARCH" section.  The existing search
options were added quickly, but were FULLY tested.

[A]lter Flags:
--------------
  This section is where you set the flags that control the userlist output.
  Enter the appropriate flag number to toggle that flag on or off.

  Whatever flags you set will be saved as defaults for the next Uni-UserList
session.

  Once you are done setting the flags, hit return to save as defaults and
then you will be taken back to the main prompt.  Hitting return here
starts the userlist.

  To abort the listing, once started, hit the "\" key or the "/" key)

  Much more work will be going into this program and I will take suggestions
regarding the flag configuration and what you wish the UserList to support
as output.  Please see the section at the bottom of this doc if you wish to
contact me regarding ANY Uni-UserList function, bug, or suggestion.

